              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "hospitālis, hospitāle — \"hospitable; of a guest or host\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Caupō hospitālis est et viātōribus bonam cēnam dat. The innkeeper is hospitable and gives the travellers a good dinner."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "An adjective of two endings, from hospes 'host, guest'. English hospital and hospitable come from the same family."
            }
          ]
        },
