          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "hospitālis is built on hospes, hospitis 'host, guest', from PIE gʰóspot- 'master of guests' (EtymDB; Lewis & Short). English hospital comes from it through French."
            }
          ]
        },
